meta {
  name: set-availability
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

patch {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/admin/v1/menu/items/{{admin_item_uid}}/availability
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{access_token}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "is_available": false
  }
}

tests {
  test("responds 200", function () {
    expect(res.status).to.equal(200)
  })

  test("flips availability without touching anything else", function () {
    expect(res.body.data.is_available).to.equal(false)
  })
}

docs {
  # Mark sold out

**The only menu route open to every staff role.** Marking a dish sold out is a floor action taken
mid-service; routing it through a manager means diners keep ordering something the kitchen ran out
of. Repricing stays owner/manager.

Separate from `update-item` so that flipping availability cannot accidentally submit a stale price
from an edit form a manager left open in another tab.

Also publishes a realtime event, so a diner with the menu open learns before checkout rather than
being rejected at it.

Set `true` to restore.
}
